{"kind":"table","sheets":["Read me","Assumptions","Transactions","Monthly summary","Where the money goes","Subscriptions & flags","Checks"],"sheet":0,"rows":[["Budget review - card spending, April to September 2026"],["Six months of your card export, categorised, summarised and checked. Every figure comes from the export itself."],[],["Prepared","2026-10-15"],["For","Richard - card account (single account, GBP)"],["Source","transactions.csv - card export from your bank, downloaded 15 Oct 2026; the original file is untouched in ~/Downloads"],["Period covered","2026-04-01 to 2026-09-30 (6 whole months, 370 transactions)"],["Currency","Pounds sterling (GBP). Amounts are as exported: card debits negative, credits positive."],["Outside figures","None. No rate, price or market data was used, so no external citation is needed."],["Method","Rules-based categorisation (Assumptions sheet); every total, average and share is a live formula, not a typed number."],[],["The three things to change"],["1. Food delivery is the leak. Takeaway and delivery cost £1,318.44 over six months (42 orders, £219.74 a month) and it is rising fast: £91.67 in April, £410.17 in August, £315.98 in September. Halving it saves about £1,320 a year."],["2. Trim the digital subscriptions. Streamly, Tunebox, CloudVault and the PixelPlay Games Pass now cost £40.96 a month (£491.52 a year) - up from £25.97 before the games pass started on 20 Jun 2026. Cancelling only the games pass frees £179.88 a year."],["3. Plan the big-ticket months. A £649 Techshack purchase in July and a £312.60 flight in September turned your two strongest months (£775 and £786 surplus) into your two weakest (£306 and £362). A standing £100-a-month sinking fund covers them without touching savings."],["Worth a look, not a change: energy (£69.53 in September, the highest month) and a £27.40 QuickBite charge that appears twice on 9 Aug 2026 - check it was not billed twice."],[],["How to read the workbook"],["Assumptions - the parameters, the category list and the merchant rules that decide every category."],["Transactions - one row per transaction; Category and Month are live formulas driven by the rules."],["Monthly summary - category x month matrix in live SUMIFS, with totals, shares and the month-by-month savings rate."],["Where the money goes - the charts."],["Subscriptions & flags - recurring charges, annualised, plus the standouts and the double-charge check."],["Checks - counts and sums that prove the workbook ties back to the export."]],"totalRows":24,"columns":2}